[MEAS] the live arm's conjunct: true
[MEAS] any KP arm — a different, real commit — moves the conjunct: false
[P4] the conjunct cannot be falsified by any recency movement (every KP arm leaves it unmoved): true
[MEAS] the CONTROL arm (empty value) moves it: true — so the leg IS reached and IS evaluable; what it cannot distinguish is WHICH commit, only WHETHER there is one.
[MEAS] therefore Theseus's "display only" is right in effect and wrong in location: the value sits INSIDE the verdict conjunction at :275, and is harmless there only because the conjunct tests presence. The published identity claim at :263 — "the fix is its own commit: <sha>" — is the reachable harm, and no leg guards it.
